WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.600
Democrats gain 258 state house seats, resetting who writes law and state capitals. This is Omni

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:13.300
View North America, episode 38. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. Still to come, a Mississippi

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:17.960
Senate count with no recount law on the books, a federal vote Thursday on the president's

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:24.380
arch, and the budget mark carney tables in Ottawa. The 258 is Chaz Nettiecombs count. He runs

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.480
state navigate, and the Guardian is where that tally appears. He also counts six new governing

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:35.580
treifectas, 11 chambers taken from Republicans, and Republican supermajorities broken in 10 states.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:40.640
Ballots are still being counted. The same reporting says Democrats have not held full control

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:47.080
of government in Arizona in 60 years, in Pennsylvania since the 1990s or in Wisconsin since 2010.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.880
Michigan and Minnesota regained treifectas they lost after the 2024 election. In Texas,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.560
Democrats will control the state house for the first time since 2002. The New York Times adds that

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:03.380
with a one control of state governments in Wisconsin, Michigan, Minnesota, Pennsylvania,

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.180
and Nevada, and won Chambers in Texas, Georgia, and North Carolina.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.860
Gubernatorial races over Republicans in Georgia, Iowa, Nevada, Ohio, and Texas put the

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.520
party in charge of a majority of governorships for the first time since 2010.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.940
Mandara Myers, who directs the state's project, calls it the most significant night for state

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:28.140
legislative power since the Republican wave of 2010, and says Democrats now have more power

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.880
in the States than at any other point in the 21st century.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:36.600
Nuddy Combe predicts about 76% of the population will live under a Democratic governor, and

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.400
about half will have a Democratic lawmaker in their legislature.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.980
He puts roughly 80% to 85% of the wave on the economy and dissatisfaction with the president.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:49.900
The Guardian says Democrats are on course for a Senate majority of at least 54 seats

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:56.140
and 237 house seats, Andy Bashir of Kentucky and Gretchen Whitmer of Michigan who lead the

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.540
Democratic Governor's Association, say more Democratic governors mean better lives for

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:05.387
the millions of Americans in their states. Mississippi is one of two Senate seats still

00:02:05.387 --> 00:02:10.167
open almost a day after Democrat secured Congress, and the Guardian has column ahead of

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:15.967
Hyde Smith by 1138 votes. Counting in Alaska is expected to run into Thursday.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:22.147
Democrat Scott column leads Republican incumbent Cindy Hyde Smith with almost 96 percent counted.

00:02:22.147 --> 00:02:27.107
His votes had been outpacing hers, then no new batches were reported for several hours.

00:02:27.627 --> 00:02:32.267
Mississippi has no law for starting a recount. The New York Times says the state does not allow

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:37.847
vote recounts in statewide elections. Democrats last won a U.S. Senate seat there in 1982.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:44.107
Donald Trump carried the state by 22 points in 2024. The state has not elected a black person

00:02:44.107 --> 00:02:50.287
to that office since 1875. Callum is a seventh-generation Mississippiian whose father was a Republican.

00:02:50.287 --> 00:02:55.747
In 2015, he became the first black district attorney for the 16th Circuit, and as district

00:02:55.747 --> 00:02:58.807
attorney, he had a 94 percent success rate for convictions.

00:02:59.932 --> 00:03:04.672
President Trump's 250-foot arch is expected to clear a federal planning board on Thursday,

00:03:05.252 --> 00:03:08.192
